<div class="review-flow-wrapper">
<figure class="review-flow" aria-labelledby="pr-review-flow-title" aria-describedby="pr-review-flow-description">
  <div class="flow-header">
    <div>
      <p class="flow-kicker">PR COUNCIL · CHECKPOINTED LANGGRAPH</p>
      <h2 id="pr-review-flow-title">One review, many independent reviewers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-status" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="status-light"></span>
      DURABLE OPERATION
    </div>
  </div>

  <p id="pr-review-flow-description" class="sr-only">
    A pull request is pinned to an immutable revision, reviewed in parallel by quality and security models,
    deliberated by disposition, and aggregated into one reconciled result. An exact preview is then held at a
    caller-controlled commit boundary before revalidation and publication.
  </p>

  <div class="flow-pipeline">
    <div class="flow-rail" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <section class="flow-stage stage-prepare" aria-labelledby="flow-prepare-title">
      <span class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-heading">
          <h3 id="flow-prepare-title">Pin and prepare the source</h3>
          <span>deterministic</span>
        </div>
        <p>Resolve context, prepare a managed worktree or validate a local checkout, and bind the operation to exact base and head commits.</p>
        <div class="revision-strip" role="group" aria-label="The review is bound to exact base and head revisions">
          <code>base_sha</code><span aria-hidden="true">···</span><code>head_sha</code><b>read-only source</b>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="flow-stage stage-review" aria-labelledby="flow-review-title">
      <span class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-heading">
          <h3 id="flow-review-title">Review in parallel</h3>
          <span>multi-model matrix</span>
        </div>
        <p>Independent model families inspect the same pinned source through bounded, read-only sandboxes.</p>
        <div class="parallel-grid">
          <div class="review-lane quality-lane">
            <div class="lane-heading"><span class="lane-shape" aria-hidden="true"></span>QUALITY</div>
            <div class="model-row" role="group" aria-label="Multiple quality reviewer models">
              <span>model 1</span><span>model 2</span><span>… n</span>
            </div>
            <div class="iteration-loop"><i aria-hidden="true">↻</i> refine findings across bounded passes</div>
          </div>
          <div class="review-lane security-lane">
            <div class="lane-heading"><span class="lane-shape" aria-hidden="true"></span>SECURITY</div>
            <div class="model-row" role="group" aria-label="Multiple security reviewer models">
              <span>model 1</span><span>model 2</span><span>… n</span>
            </div>
            <div class="iteration-loop"><i aria-hidden="true">↻</i> refine findings across bounded passes</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="flow-stage stage-deliberate" aria-labelledby="flow-deliberate-title">
      <span class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-heading">
          <h3 id="flow-deliberate-title">Deliberate by disposition</h3>
          <span>closed set</span>
        </div>
        <p>Each council must decide the exact findings its reviewers produced: retain or reject, never invent.</p>
        <div class="decision-grid" role="group" aria-label="Quality and security deliberations happen in parallel">
          <div><span class="decision-input">quality findings</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span class="decision-output">quality verdicts</span></div>
          <div><span class="decision-input">security findings</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span class="decision-output">security verdicts</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="flow-stage stage-aggregate" aria-labelledby="flow-aggregate-title">
      <span class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-heading">
          <h3 id="flow-aggregate-title">Aggregate the signal</h3>
          <span>one reconciled result</span>
        </div>
        <p>Merge overlap, preserve source-finding IDs, carry forward the strongest severity, and produce one reconciled review.</p>
        <div class="funnel" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Q</span><span>S</span><i></i><strong>REVIEW</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="flow-stage stage-approve" aria-labelledby="flow-approve-title">
      <span class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
      <div class="stage-card gate-card">
        <div class="stage-heading">
          <h3 id="flow-approve-title">Preview, then wait</h3>
          <span>caller-controlled gate</span>
        </div>
        <p>Build the exact payload and hash. The caller can commit matching values or cancel; cancellation closes once publication begins.</p>
        <div class="approval-row">
          <div><small>BOUND TO</small><code>revision + payload hash</code></div>
          <span class="wait-state"><i></i> CALLER: COMMIT / CANCEL</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="flow-stage stage-publish" aria-labelledby="flow-publish-title">
      <span class="stage-marker" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-heading">
          <h3 id="flow-publish-title">Revalidate and publish</h3>
          <span>replay-safe</span>
        </div>
        <p>Recheck the PR revision, payload, identity, and duplicate state at the side-effect boundary.</p>
        <div class="terminal-row">
          <span class="terminal-success">INLINE COMMENTS + COMMENT SUMMARY</span>
          <span class="terminal-muted">or stale → no publish</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <figcaption>Progress is checkpointed throughout. The caller can poll, preview, commit, or cancel, and the runtime can recover after a restart.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>

